System partition encryption key

File format
  system.key: Exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters representing a 32-byte
  AES key, with no newline. This is not a 64-byte binary key. File mode must be 0600.

Generate a key
  Run these commands in a new, empty directory. Do not overwrite an existing key.

  umask 077
  openssl rand -hex 32 | tr -d '\n' > system.key
  chmod 600 system.key
  test "$(wc -c < system.key)" -eq 64

Usage
  The build encrypts the system SquashFS with this key and places its initial
  import record in misc. On first boot, TEE/HUK wraps the key into a blob, stores
  it in misc and clears the plaintext import record. No TA UUID is required.
  The device generates the userdata key with TEE Trusted Keys, separately from
  system.key. System OTA bundles for existing devices must use the same key that
  those devices can unwrap.
